Description: avfilter/tonemapx: keep one Dolby Vision mapping instead of one per frame
 For every frame whose reshaping it applies, tonemapx allocated a
 struct FFDOVIMetadataRemap, stored its address in the filter context
 over the address of the previous frame's, and freed only the last one
 when the filter closed. Each such frame left 2,728 bytes allocated and
 unreachable. At 24 frames per second that is 225 MB (of 2^20 bytes)
 for each hour of video. The frames are those with RPU profile 0 and
 no enhancement layer residual, profile 5 among them.
 .
 Allocate the struct when the first such frame arrives and map every
 later frame's metadata into it. ff_map_dovi_metadata() writes every
 field that the reshaping of a frame reads: the two matrices and the
 offset, the number of pivots, and for each piece its pivots, its
 method and that method's coefficients. So the output does not change.
 .
 tonemap_cuda, tonemap_opencl and tonemap_videotoolbox free the struct
 after each frame. tonemapx cannot: once it has seen such a frame it
 keeps the Dolby Vision path for every later frame and reads the last
 mapping there, so the struct stays until the filter closes, as the
 last frame's did before.
 .
 A failed allocation now returns ENOMEM. Before, the frame was dropped
 and the filter returned success.
